llama: stage no-mmap weight loads through one bounded buffer

Without mmap and without an async upload backend, load_all_data reads every tensor
into its own std::vector sized like the tensor, then ggml_backend_tensor_set. On iOS
Metal has no host buffer type, so every weight takes this path, and the freed
vectors park in libmalloc's deferred reclaim ring: 56 MiB after a 350M model and
221 MiB after granite 3B stay in phys_footprint, and the next in-process
max_memory_usage cell starts on top of them. The per-tensor vectors also add the
largest tensor to the load's own peak.

Stage through ONE ggml_aligned_malloc buffer (vm_allocate on iOS with 002) of
min(16 MiB, largest staged tensor): read and tensor_set in chunks, free it after the
loop. Host buffers keep the direct read. CPU_REPACK buffers (not host, and their
set_tensor takes a tensor only whole) keep the per-tensor vector. check_tensors, mmap
and upload_backend loads are untouched.

Applied at build time by ios/build-llama.sh after 002. Remove once upstreamed to
ggml-org.
